    },
    {
      "id": "call-07",
      "startedAt": "2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z",
      "durationS": 363,
      "status": "done",
      "summary": "Hal shared his Steelers memories, including watching the Immaculate Reception on a borrowed TV in 1972. He thinks this year’s team needs a better offensive line.",
      "photosShown": [],
      "familyQuestion": null,
      "mood": "positive",
      "isSimulated": true
    },
    {
      "id": "call-06",
      "startedAt": "2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z",
      "durationS": 517,
      "status": "done",
      "summary": "Hal talked about playing trumpet in the Hollidaysburg High marching band and the cold November games. He hummed part of the fight song and said he can still play a few bars of \"Beer Barrel Polka.\"",
      "photosShown": [],
      "familyQuestion": null,
      "mood": "positive",
      "isSimulated": true
    },
    {
      "id": "call-05",
      "startedAt": "2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z",
      "durationS": 566,
      "status": "done",
      "summary": "Hal told the story of meeting Dorothy at a church dance in 1964. He said she stepped on his foot before he ever asked her to dance, and he married her two years later. He got quiet for a moment, then said she would have liked these chats.",
      "photosShown": [
        {
          "id": "p-lake",
          "caption": "Hal and Mom at Raystown Lake, 1980"
        }
      ],
      "familyQuestion": {
        "text": "How did you meet Mom?",
        "askedBy": "Linda",
        "answer": "At a church dance in 1964 — she stepped on his foot first."
      },
      "mood": "neutral",
      "isSimulated": true
    },
    {
      "id": "call-04",
      "startedAt": "2026-09-28T14:00:00.000Z",
      "durationS": 637,
      "status": "done",
      "summary": "Looking at the photo from the shops, Hal named three of the men he worked beside and told how they rebuilt a K4 locomotive for a museum. He was proud the engine still runs on special excursions.",
